ShareVaultSettleEpochTest
├── when the caller is not the nav receiver
│   └── it should revert
├── when the close id is not the current epoch
│   └── it should revert
├── when the report is observed in the future
│   └── it should revert
├── when the report is older than the max report age
│   └── it should revert
├── when the report is not newer than the last settlement
│   └── it should revert
├── when the report is newer than the last settlement
│   └── it should be accepted
├── when the liabilities consume all assets
│   └── it should revert
├── given the price moves beyond the deviation bound
│   ├── given the deviation was not acknowledged
│   │   └── it should pause requests and keep the epoch open
│   ├── given the deviation was acknowledged
│   │   ├── it should keep requests paused until the next settlement
│   │   └── it should settle and clear the acknowledgement
│   └── given a later report is back inside the bound
│       └── it should settle and unpause
└── given the price is inside the deviation bound
    ├── given the share supply is zero
    │   ├── it should price at the opening price
    │   └── given assets remain after the last redemption
    │       └── it should mint them to the fee recipient so the next depositor pays a fair price
    ├── given a deposit is pending after a loss
    │   └── it should not let the late depositor capture the loss
    ├── given a deposit is pending after a gain
    │   └── it should not let the late depositor capture the gain
    ├── given a redemption within the liquidity cap
    │   └── it should pay at the close price
    ├── given redemptions beyond the liquidity cap
    │   └── it should fill pro rata and roll the remainder into the next epoch
    ├── given redemptions beyond the cash held on Arc
    │   └── it should cap the fill by the cash held
    ├── given the price is above the high water mark
    │   └── it should mint a performance fee in shares
    └── given the price is below the high water mark
        └── it should mint no fee and keep the high water mark
